{"version":3,"kind":"Notebook","sha256":"27caeea5bc8009f4e622d3264b6ce3e14699fe3136fde1f8cea8faf075a5cc18","slug":"notebooks.downscaling-overview","location":"/notebooks/09_downscaling_overview.ipynb","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"Temporal downscaling: 6h native steps to 1h","content_includes_title":false,"kernelspec":{"name":"e2s-gpu","display_name":"e2s-gpu","language":"python"},"jupytext":{},"authors":[{"nameParsed":{"literal":"cgroll","family":"cgroll"},"name":"cgroll","id":"contributors-myst-generated-uid-0"}],"github":"https://github.com/cgroll/e2s-examples","copyright":"2026","numbering":{"title":{"offset":1}},"source_url":"https://github.com/cgroll/e2s-examples/blob/main/book/notebooks/09_downscaling_overview.ipynb","edit_url":"https://github.com/cgroll/e2s-examples/edit/main/book/notebooks/09_downscaling_overview.ipynb","thumbnail":"/e2s-examples/build/meteogram_t2m_munich-11b60a6211450a558671dfb800fc7d22.png","exports":[{"format":"ipynb","filename":"09_downscaling_overview.ipynb","url":"/e2s-examples/build/09_downscaling_overv-8a752e4794417b11975550b85abeff61.ipynb"}]},"widgets":{},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-content","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"InterpModAFNO","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"V2FlGePqxm"},{"type":"text","value":" wraps SFNO (a 6h-native prognostic model) and inserts 5\nAFNO-interpolated steps between each pair of SFNO’s own 6h outputs,\nproducing an hourly forecast. Crucially, the steps at the 6h boundaries\naren’t touched by the interpolation model - they’re SFNO’s own output,\npassed straight through. So within the single hourly zarr this experiment\nwrites, every 6th lead-time step is a genuine model prediction and\neverything in between is AFNO-synthesized.","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"OJMBs9Qpd0"}],"key":"MBV03Be45t"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":11,"column":1},"end":{"line":14,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"This chapter compares the two directly: the same field, the same\nrollout, once at native 6h resolution and once at the interpolated 1h\nresolution - stacked so the added temporal detail (and which of it is\n“real”) is visible at a glance.","position":{"start":{"line":11,"column":1},"end":{"line":11,"column":1}},"key":"jgDs41Itt0"}],"key":"QLQQ1DrAWO"}],"key":"gHDvNhXj9r"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-code","data":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-07-27T08:42:59.317735Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-07-27T08:42:59.317622Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-07-27T08:42:59.452560Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-07-27T08:42:59.452193Z"}},"children":[{"type":"code","lang":"python","executable":true,"value":"import shutil\n\nimport matplotlib\nmatplotlib.use(\"Agg\")\n\nfrom e2s.paths import ProjPaths\n\npaths = ProjPaths()\npaths.ensure_directories()\n\n\ndef copy_asset(src, dst):\n    if src.exists():\n        shutil.copyfile(src, dst)\n        print(f\"Copied {src} -> {dst}\")\n    else:\n        print(f\"[WARN] {src} not found - run 02_analyse.py first.\")","key":"chBT2N18eK"},{"type":"outputs","id":"y62CeVwB33a9Qb3VZEPpT","children":[],"key":"LPqw0ZQczA"}],"key":"og5v1dcdYL"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-content","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Munich meteogram: dense vs. native-only","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"GSriUlc334"}],"identifier":"munich-meteogram-dense-vs-native-only","label":"Munich meteogram: dense vs. native-only","html_id":"munich-meteogram-dense-vs-native-only","implicit":true,"key":"b1IRNItfhc"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The hourly boxplot below has roughly 6x as many x-axis entries as the\nnative-only one directly beneath it - same rollout, same member spread,\njust far more temporal detail. The orange boxes in the top panel mark\nthe steps that are SFNO’s own native 6h output; the grey boxes around\nthem are AFNO-interpolated.","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"RIEUYmILqh"}],"key":"QxHTl0znpW"}],"key":"NLemCWLutV"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-code","data":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-07-27T08:42:59.454818Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-07-27T08:42:59.454649Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-07-27T08:42:59.459106Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-07-27T08:42:59.458455Z"}},"children":[{"type":"code","lang":"python","executable":true,"value":"copy_asset(\n    paths.downscaling_analysis_path / \"meteogram_t2m_munich_dense.png\",\n    paths.downscaling_book_path / \"meteogram_t2m_munich_dense.png\",\n)\ncopy_asset(\n    paths.downscaling_analysis_path / \"meteogram_t2m_munich_native.png\",\n    paths.downscaling_book_path / \"meteogram_t2m_munich_native.png\",\n)","key":"tz52WZLaxA"},{"type":"outputs","id":"tNF7DUfFt5kQ0cG2mH1z1","children":[{"type":"output","jupyter_data":{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":"Copied /root/e2s-examples/output/downscaling/analysis/meteogram_t2m_munich_dense.png -> /root/e2s-examples/output/downscaling/book/meteogram_t2m_munich_dense.png\nCopied /root/e2s-examples/output/downscaling/analysis/meteogram_t2m_munich_native.png -> /root/e2s-examples/output/downscaling/book/meteogram_t2m_munich_native.png\n"},"children":[],"key":"NNcjPa3TLp"}],"key":"wnw5NuVlKo"}],"key":"lclTMqNHym"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-content","children":[{"type":"container","kind":"figure","children":[{"type":"image","url":"/e2s-examples/build/meteogram_t2m_munich-11b60a6211450a558671dfb800fc7d22.png","alt":"Munich 2m temperature ensemble meteogram, hourly resolution. Orange boxes\nare native SFNO steps; grey boxes